      "content": "That lump sounds like a minor infection, and ibuprofen and warm compresses are a great start. You can try applying a warm compress for 10-15 minutes, 3-4 times a day, to help bring the pus to the surface and encourage it to drain. I recommend taking an additional dose of ibuprofen, but make sure to take it with a glass of water and not with any food, to maximize absorption. If the pain persists or the lump doesn't show signs of draining within 24 hours, you might want to consider a quick trip to the pharmacy for some antibiotic ointment.",
